From f5ed8c97f97acdfe39a186edbe1fb770ea8e1070 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:09:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): an unused Board grant does not spend a parked
 owner's review continuation [daveey]

resumes_review, the owner-wake hold release and the guard notice selected the
card's newest run row (MAX(id)). A Board grant returned unused adds a newer
'released' row that ran nothing, so a finished exact-head review no longer
resumed its owner and active_pr held it until the PR merged. They now use
latest_started_run, as the ordering-dependency handoff has since 6e0d3134b35.
Any started, failed or unattested run still consumes the continuation.
---
